  "script": "With its rally roots, this one offered performance in a practical package. Today, they go for about $19,500. Not bad considering its pedigree. Subaru's WRX first graced U.S. shores in 2001, capturing the spirit of World Rally. Its 2.0L turbocharged flat-four pushes 227 horsepower and 217 lb-ft of torque. The AWD system ensures superior grip and handling. This WRX comes with a 5-speed manual, perfectly paired with the viscous limited-slip differential. That combination delivers power smoothly to all four wheels. It\u2019s an enthusiast's delight. Rivaling the Audi A4 Avant in utility, the WRX shines with performance. The WRX\u2019s 227 hp beats the A4 Avant's 170 hp. But the Audi offers a more luxurious interior. So, is this wagon about practicality or performance? Would you take rally genes over luxury for your daily drive?",
