      "Highlights": "THIS...is a 2002 Subaru Impreza WRX Wagon, finished in Platinum Silver Metallic with a blue and gray interior. This WRX is equipped with the desirable 5-speed manual transmission, and the odometer indicates approximately 49,500 miles. The attached Carfax history report lists no accidents or odometer discrepancies in this Subaru's past. It also lists just one North Carolina owner from new. Factory equipment on this WRX includes a viscous limited-slip rear differential, a sport-tuned suspension system, cloth upholstery, a leather-wrapped MOMO steering wheel, a boost gauge, air conditioning, and a CD player. The selling dealer reports no modifications. The 2nd-generation Impreza made its debut for the 2001 model year, and it spawned the first WRX sold on the American market. Like the standard Impreza, the WRX was offered as a sedan and as a station wagon. The WRX (World Rally eXperimental) gained rally-bred upgrades including a more powerful engine, a firmer suspension, and a more muscular-looking design characterized by a functional hood scoop and a rear spoiler. Power comes from a 2.0-liter turbocharged flat 4 engine, rated at 227 horsepower and 217 lb-ft. Output is sent to all 4 wheels through a 5-speed manual transmission.",
